## Input

```mlk
// Paths of types, qualified and applied to type arguments, and the types a module leaves to
// be inferred. A name a type is rooted at is a name of the module, so the types the paths
// name are declared here.

#[builtin]
type Map

#[builtin]
type String

fun qualified(value: std::core::Int): Unit =
    value

fun applied(value: Map[Int, String]): Unit =
    value

fun applied_and_qualified(value: std::Map[Int, String,]): Unit =
    value

fun applied_to_a_qualified_path(value: std::core::Map[Int, String]): Unit =
    value

// A name read inside the type a path applies an argument to: the argument is written at the
// root of the path, and what follows it is read inside the type it makes.
fun applied_and_read_inside(value: Map[Int]::Entry): Unit =
    value

fun inferred(value: _): _ =
    value

```

